            <ArticleTitle>[A young woman with abnormal vaginal tissue loss].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A9515</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 18-year-old woman experienced abnormal and painful vaginal tissue loss while using an oral contraceptive. A pregnancy test was negative. Histopathological examination of the tissue showed a decidualised endometrium. We made the diagnosis of progesterone-induced membranous dysmenorrhoea.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
